Having just completed a major battle with a giant mummy, one in which my
eighth-level barbarian had to call on Crom for help with hitpoints, I
decided it couldn't hurt -too- much to eat the corpse.  Tainted meat, natch.
(Mummies seem to be about 50/50 on this call.)  No problem, thinks I.  I
try to sneak in a prayer to Crom in case he's not all that ticked off at
me.  No dice.  Okay, so I resort to plan (b): whip out the ol' blessed magic
lamp I picked up in the tool shop and make a wish.  One #rub later, I have
a djinni ready and willing to grant me a wish.  I know exactly what I
want: "blessed unicorn horn".  Poof!  I have my wish, and the djinni flits
off for parts unknown.  Wasting no time, I (a)pply the unicorn horn.  Nothing
happens.  Blink.  Did I hit the wrong key?  We'll try again.  (a)pply (c).
I go blind.  Blind?  What?!  Desperate, I take one more step, and die.  Sure
enough, in my inventory, 1 (one) cursed +0 unicorn horn.

*cough*  What?  I asked for it to be blessed!  I want a refund!

Seriously, what happened to the 'blessed' part of it?
